<main class="pc" data-product-depth="cases"><p class="pc-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS / Cases</p><h1>Changes we can describe and compare.</h1><p class="pc-lead">Explore practitioner-reported archive observations with their context and provenance intact.</p><section class="pc-section"><h2>Archive narratives</h2><div class="pc-feature"><p class="pc-kicker">Practitioner report · primary records not published</p><h3>01 · Neck</h3><div class="pc-metrics"><div class="pc-metric"><strong>−3</strong><span>Initial rating</span></div><div class="pc-metric"><strong>+7</strong><span>Subsequent rating</span></div></div><p>Four visits. According to the practitioner, habitual neck cracking was no longer reported; the author's scale changed from −3 to +7.</p><p class="pc-note">Author's scale; range and primary questionnaire are not provided in the archive entry. Not a clinical scale.</p><details><summary>02 · Shoulder</summary><p>A shoulder issue lasting about eighteen months. The practitioner reported approximately 80% subjective improvement after one session.</p></details><details><summary>03 · Visible symmetry</summary><p>An archive summary describes observed changes in facial symmetry over 1.5–2 months after 2–5 sessions; this is not an individual photographic record.</p></details><p class="pc-note">Primary measurements, photographs and participant permissions are not included in the public archive. The numbers do not predict another individual's outcome.</p></div></section><section class="pc-section"><h2>Record architecture</h2><div class="pc-record"><div><b>01</b>Initial request</div><div><b>02</b>Context and work</div><div><b>03</b>Observations and measurements</div><div><b>04</b>Follow-up and verification</div></div><div class="pc-actions"><a class="pc-button primary" href="../your-cranium/">Explore your own context ↗</a><a class="pc-button" href="../twinmind/">TwinMind</a><a class="pc-button" href="../start/">Discuss your individual enquiry</a></div></section><section class="pc-section"><details class="pc-legacy"><summary>Existing archive materials</summary><div class="commercial"><div class="wrap"><article class="cr-detail"><p class="cr-kicker">CRANIO SYSTEMS / Observation archive</p><h2>Case observations: what can be verified</h2><p class="cr-lead">The archive includes practitioner-reported changes in tension, movement and visible symmetry. These reports are kept separate from validated evidence.</p><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-primary" href="../start/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-booking="email">Discuss your individual enquiry</a><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="../">Back to homepage</a></div>
<section class="cr-section"><h2>Themes in individual observations</h2><p class="cr-intro">These are archive themes, not three independently verified clinical cases. Every future public record will require source materials and appropriate consent.</p><div class="cr-three"><div class="cr-card"><h3>Neck tension</h3><p>Individual reports of a change in perceived tension and comfort after soft-tissue work.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>Head mobility</h3><p>Observations of differences in ease of movement that require comparable pre/post measurements.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>Visible symmetry</h3><p>Photographic observations requiring consistent framing, lighting and independent review.</p></div></div></section><section class="cr-section"><h2>What a case record must contain</h2><div class="cr-steps"><div class="cr-card"><h3>Baseline</h3><p>Participant's own description and date.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>Intervention</h3><p>Type of work, session count and limitations.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>Outcomes</h3><p>Measurements, observations and participant reports separately.</p></div><div class="cr-card"><h3>Follow-up</h3><p>Later observations, including adverse effects.</p></div></div><p class="cr-small">Historical marketing numbers without original measurements are not presented as verified evidence. Session counts are not the same as validated case counts.</p></section>
<section class="cr-section cr-safety"><h2>Safety and limitations</h2><p>CRANIO is a nonmedical practice, not a substitute for diagnosis or treatment. Sudden severe headache, numbness, weakness, speech or vision disturbances or pain after injury require urgent medical assessment. External observations do not prove C0–C1 bone displacement, and outcomes are not guaranteed.</p></section>
<section class="cr-finale"><h2>Have a question about your situation?</h2><p>Contact the practitioner to discuss the session format and availability.</p><div class="cr-actions"><a class="cr-button cr-primary" href="../start/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" data-booking="email">Discuss your individual enquiry</a><a class="cr-button cr-outline" href="../#safety">About safety</a></div></section></article></div></div></details></section></main>